msgid "Bring a file into a room"
msgstr ""

msgid "*Bring the file you are working on into a new room.*"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"A study you have on your disk can become a room: EMStudio creates the "
"room, sends the files the graph cites, puts the graph in the room and "
"enters it. From that moment the live copy of the study is the room's. "
"Your file stays where it was, unchanged, and keeping a copy on the disk "
"later is a separate gesture."
msgstr ""

msgid "Before you start"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Open the study from its ``.em.json`` (see :doc:`/how-to/files/open-save-"
"recent`). The files the graph cites with a relative path are looked for "
"in the folder of the ``.em.json``, and in the DosCo folders the file "
"declares."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Do the three steps of the chip's menu at the top right: an **Author**, a "
"**Node** that answers, and **Sign in** on it (see :doc:`sign-in`). If one"
" is missing, the gesture opens the menu at that step and goes on by "
"itself once it is done."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The files are read where they are on your computer, by EMStudio's local "
"service, the bridge. The desktop application starts its own. In the web "
"version, the page needs a bridge running on your computer: without one, "
"the window below stops with **The room importer stopped:** and the "
"reason."
msgstr ""

msgid "Create the room with the study in it"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Choose ``File ▸ Bring this into a new room…``. The same command is "
"**Bring into a room…** in the section **My space** of the chip's menu."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The dialog **Bring this into a new room** asks for the room's name, for "
"example «Templu Mare 2026». Press **Create and put it there**."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The window **Resources of the graph → room**, followed by the name, opens"
" and says **Creating the room and reading what the graph cites…**. Then "
"it shows the files of the study in five groups, each with the number of "
"files and their size:"
msgstr ""

msgid "**Found on this computer**"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The files that will be sent. For each one choose **Upload** (the "
"default), **Leave as a reference** or **Skip**. **All of them:** sets the"
" choice for the whole group, and the line that ends in **files, one by "
"one** opens the list file by file. A folder of tiles (a 3D Tiles tileset)"
" goes up as one ``.3tz`` file."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Already in the room's storage**"
msgstr ""

msgid "Files the node already holds with the same content: nothing is sent again."
msgstr ""

msgid "**At home in another room**"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Files already on the node, kept by another room. By default this room "
"hosts them as they are (**Host it here (its home stays)**). **Move here**"
" brings them under this room, and their rights become this room's; "
"**Leave as a reference** keeps them as a reference to the other room."
msgstr ""

msgid "**External references (NAS, URL)**"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Addresses that are not files of this computer: counted and left as they "
"are."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Missing**"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Paths that cannot be found: counted, named and left. To find them first, "
"see :doc:`/how-to/files/find-missing-files`."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Photographs taken in one session appear as a **Proposed lot**. Tick **one"
" lot (one acquisition)** to record them as a single acquisition."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Read the line **To upload:**, with the number of files and their size, "
"and press **Upload**. If you chose **Move here** for some files, a "
"confirmation lists the rooms they leave and the rooms whose graphs will "
"cite them as a reference; answer **Move here** or **Leave them as "
"references**."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The window shows the progress (**Sending ·** the bytes sent of the "
"total). **Pause** stops the upload between two pieces and **Resume** "
"takes it up again."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"To stop before anything is sent, press **Later**: the room exists and is "
"empty, and the graph is not in it. Choosing ``File ▸ Bring this into a "
"new room…`` again with the same name takes it up again."
msgstr ""

msgid "What you get"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"A new room on the node with the graph in it and you as its **owner**. The"
" window ends with one line, **Uploaded** … **already in the storage** … "
"**references** … **missing** …, and the link to the room on the node."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"EMStudio enters the room: the status bar reads **Room**, followed by the "
"name of the room and of the node, and the graph you see is the room's "
"copy."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"What goes up is visible only to the room's participants, unless its "
"resource node (or its lot) says otherwise."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Your ``.em.json`` on the disk is unchanged. To keep a copy of the room's "
"study on your disk, use ``File ▸ Save As…``."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"If a room with that name already exists on the node, it is taken up again"
" only when you are its owner or an admin, as after **Later**. For anybody"
" else the window stops and says that only its owner takes it up again: "
"enter that room instead, or choose another name."
msgstr ""

msgid "Send more files later"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Inside a room, **Resources of the room…** in the section **Where you "
"work** of the chip's menu opens the same window for the room you are in, "
"for its owner and its admins: the files the graph cites that the room "
"already holds appear under **Already in the room's storage**, and the "
"others can be sent as above."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Files can also be deposited in the room by hand, as one lot with its "
"licence and its author: in the **Archive** workspace, switch the "
"**Files** window to the mode **In the room**, sign the delivery and drop "
"the files (see :doc:`/how-to/archive/storage`)."
msgstr ""

msgid "Declare a derivation"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"In the same mode **In the room**, the form **Declare a derivation** "
"records that a resource came out of others: an orthophoto out of a flight"
" of photographs, a mesh out of a lot. Nothing is guessed from dates or "
"names: the derivation is what you declare. The form appears once the "
"study has documentation (lots or resources), also when you are not in a "
"room."
msgstr ""

msgid "In **Output**, pick the resource that resulted."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"In **Inputs**, pick what it came from: the lots first (marked ▣), then "
"single resources. Several can be picked together."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"In **Tool**, write the name of the program, for example Metashape, "
"Blender or QGIS. The name is enough."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Press **Declare**. The panel's trail says that the output is declared as "
"derived from its inputs."
msgstr ""

msgid "See also"
msgstr ""

msgid ":doc:`create-a-room`, to create an empty room."
msgstr ""

msgid ":doc:`enter-and-share-a-room`, to invite the people of the project."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
":doc:`/how-to/sources/declare-provenance`, for stamps and the "
"transformation chain of the files on disk."
msgstr ""

msgid ":doc:`/explanation/open-enter-create`, on where the copy you edit lives."
msgstr ""

